BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Holiday Herbal Gift Making at Made Local
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T130000
UID:261103v6mMMdXZxkSE3p5qxU17hQ
DESCRIPTION:Join Oleum Botanicals for an enchanting afternoon of blending\
 , brewing\, and crafting. In this immersive workshop\, you will learn the 
 art of transforming simple\, organic botanicals into beautiful\, heartfelt
  holiday gifts. Guided by Kate Furtner\, RN and Clinical Nurse-Herbalist\,
  we will bridge modern wellness with traditional plant wisdom. Together\, 
 we will craft a few master creations in class\, and you will leave equippe
 d with a comprehensive recipe packet and the step-by-step master skills to
  confidently hand-make all your holiday gifts at home!\n\nThe Workshop Cur
 riculum: • The Kitchen Apothecary: Infused honeys\, artisan culinary sal
 ts\, aromatic oils\, homemade extracts\, and festive seasonal teas & cocoa
 s. • Bath & Body Rituals: Nourishing bath salts\, exfoliating sugar and 
 lip scrubs\, infused body oils\, and fragrant herbal dream pillows. • Se
 asonal Home Accents: Beautiful herbal garlands and botanical plant wands t
 o bring nature indoors.\n\nWhat’s Included: • Live\, expert guidance f
 rom a clinical nurse-herbalist. • Materials to craft a few select botani
 cal items during the workshop. • A comprehensive\, take-home recipe and 
 instruction booklet to recreate the entire gift collection at your own pac
 e. No experience necessary—this workshop is beginner-friendly. Kate’s 
 relationship with medicinal plants began in childhood\, rooted in the land
 scapes of Northern California. Her lifelong passion led her to study ethno
 botany at the University of Hawaii\, followed by years of exploring tradit
 ional herbal medicine throughout South America\, New Zealand\, Australia\,
  and Fiji. Now based in Sonoma County\, Kate brings a unique blend of clin
 ical expertise and ancestral plant wisdom to her work\, balancing life as 
 an ER nurse\, clinical nurse-herbalist\, and mother of three. She grows ma
 ny of the herbs used in her formulations\, creating small-batch organic re
 medies and body-care products that bridge modern healthcare with holistic\
 , earth-based healing. www.Oleumbotanicals.com\n\nWorkshop fee includes al
 l materials and a take-home custom tea blend\, plus a step-by-step guide.\
 n\nImportant Notes: • Advance registration required • Workshops requir
 e a minimum of 4 participants • 72 hours notice required for a partial r
 efund •Workshops are held outdoors but undercover at Made Local Marketpl
 ace in Montgomery Village
LOCATION:Made Local
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/holiday-herbal-gift-making-at-ma
 de-local/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ARTIST RECEPTION Just Around The Corner - Paintings by Bill Gittin
 s
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
UID:261103tLeEdaKCcU-_Ok6TqB6mpA
DESCRIPTION:Meet the Artist Reception Saturday\, November 7th from Noon - 
 4pm at Rena Charles Gallery located at 439 Healdsburg Ave\, Healdsburg.\n\
 nJust Around The Corner - Palette knife paintings by Bill Gittins\n\nRoote
 d in the landscape of Sonoma County\, Bill Gittins paints with an eye for 
 color\, movement\, and the energy of a passing moment. Working in oil with
  both brush and palette knife\, he finds his subjects close to home: viney
 ards and rolling hills\, country roads and winding trails\, weathered barn
 s\, coastal bluffs\, crashing waves and retreating tides\, and skies that 
 shift from drifting clouds to blazing sunsets. These scenes become more th
 an features of the natural world\; they invite the eye to wander and the i
 magination to follow. Like the paths we take in life\, his roads and trail
 s lead toward possibilities just out of view\, and toward whatever waits a
 round the next bend.
LOCATION:Rena Charles Gallery
URL:http://www.renacharlesgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art FREE Nov 7-8 Bank of America Museums o
 n Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T170000
UID:261102z8Dfgzl3s0KDvRAz8ofEwA
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is November 7-8. \n\nWith Thanksgiving and winter just around
  the corner\, the late fall season means just one thing: it’s the perfec
 t time for some indoor fun at your local museum! The Sonoma Valley Museum 
 of Art has exciting exhibits including brand new installation The Real-Lif
 e Art History of M. Louise Stanley\, an exhibit sponsored by Bank of Ameri
 ca that celebrates a unique Bay Area Figurative artist for her wildly imag
 inative narratives and distinctly female perspective\, shaped by her keen 
 observations of everyday life and setting her apart from her male contempo
 raries. The exhibit features Sanley’s large-scale acrylic paintings\, go
 uache and watercolor works on paper\, sculptural objects\, sketchbooks\, s
 tudies\, photos\, and notes from her personal archives\, showing the artis
 t’s perspective across multiple media forms. \n\nBank of America Museum
 s on Us program offers FREE weekend general admission on the first full we
 ekend of every month to Bank of America\, Merrill and Bank of America Priv
 ate Bank credit and debit cardholders. All you need is your Bank of Americ
 a\, Merrill\, or Bank of America Private Bank card and picture ID for acce
 ss. \n\nAdditional participating museums can be found here: https://about
 .bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-partner
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
