UID:261029-xmjTzbBeUe_tFm3MbqZBg
DESCRIPTION:The parents of children at St. Paul's Episcopal Church in Heal
 dsburg are sponsoring an Upcycle Clothing Event at the church parish hall 
 on Saturday\, Nov. 7\, from 12-4 p.m. Everyone is invited to come by the h
 all at 209 Matheson Street\, grab a grocery-size bag\, pay a fee of $20 an
 d fill the bag with all the clothing\, shoes\, books\, toys and other chil
 dren's items it will hold. All of the items are gently-used and have been 
 collected and sorted by the parents of the kids who attend St. Paul's. Mos
 t items are gently used but some are practically new and have simply been 
 outgrown. A few particularly dressy items will be separately priced. Proce
 eds from the sale will be used to fund children's activities at the church
 \, such as buying art supplies for the newly-refurbished Sunday School roo
 m. That room will be open during the sale for children to visit while thei
 r parents shop. Members of the Episcopal Church Women will assist with the
  sale.
LOCATION:St. Paul's Episcopal Church parish hall
URL:http://www.stpauls-healdsburg.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Park Admission for Veterans and Active Military
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T170000
UID:261028bdeqzwTfGUaya8LmvrbIJQ
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of their service to the United States\, Jack Lo
 ndon State Historic Park will provide free admission to all active-duty mi
 litary and veterans on Nov. 7\, 8\, 9\, 10\, and 11 - Veterans Day – 202
 6.\n\nBlending the fascinating history of one of America’s most prolific
  and successful writers with the serenity of nature\, Jack London State Hi
 storic Park offers more than 29 miles of back-country trails that roam thr
 ough mixed forests\, redwood groves\, oak woodlands\, and grassy meadows i
 n Sonoma County’s Valley of the Moon.  \n\nActive duty or retired mili
 tary identification or form DD214 can be presented at the entry kiosk to r
 eceive free admission.\n\nAdmission\, regularly priced at $15\, covers one
  vehicle of up to nine passengers for the day.  Park hours are 9 a.m. to 
 5 p.m. daily.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Oak Grove Picnic Area (standing
  capacity)
URL:http://www.jacklondonpark.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
