DESCRIPTION:Tod Dickow is “one of the best saxophonists in the world” 
 according to Jazz Life Magazine\, and his playing has been recognized by o
 utstanding soloist awards at the Pacific Coast Jazz Festival and the Outst
 anding Soloist award from Down Beat Magazine.  He has appeared with numero
 us celebrated artists\, including Ella Fitzgerald\, Nancy Wilson\, Joe Hen
 derson\, Bobby Hutcherson\, Jackie & Roy\, Harry Connick Jr\, Steve Allen\
 , Terry Gibbs\, Frank Sinatra Jr.\, Dave Brubeck\, and many more.\n\nRevie
 wers have called Charged Particles “a tight and enormously talented trio
 .” \\(Jazz Times Magazine\\) that is “definitely dazzling” \\(Jazz a
 nd Blues Report\\) and plays “fresh\, energized jazz that showcases the 
 trio’s individual technical mastery.” \\(Jazz News Magazine\\) with 
 “tight interplay\, spark\, and personal flair.” \\(Los Angeles Times\\
 ).  Downbeat Magazine called their performance at the famed club Birdland 
 “something special: inventive\, invigorating\, mesmerizing\, and virtuos
 ic.”
LOCATION:4th Corner Speakeasy
