BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Book of Will\, a dramatic comedy presented by Solano College T
 heatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T213000
UID:261023GbmOcPgcIUefcedkzn6u6g
DESCRIPTION:Solano College Theatre presents\n\nThe Book of Will\n\n📆Nov
 ember 6-22\, 2026\n\n📌4000 Suisun Valley Road\, Fairfield CA\n\n🎟 Ti
 ckets: www.solanocollegetheatre.org\n\n📞 \\(707\\) 864-7100\n\nWhere th
 ere’s a will\, there’s a way.\n\n“The Book of Will” brings to life
  the chaotic\, hilarious\, passionate\, and mostly true endeavor to compil
 e Shakespeare’s plays into the legendary First Folio!\n\nAbout the show:
  Without William Shakespeare\, we wouldn’t have literary masterpieces li
 ke “Romeo and Juliet.” But without Henry Condell and John Heminges\, w
 e would have lost half of Shakespeare’s plays forever! After the death o
 f their friend and mentor\, the two actors are determined to compile the F
 irst Folio and preserve the words that shaped their lives. They’ll just 
 have to borrow\, beg\, and band together to get it done. Amidst the noise 
 and color of Elizabethan London\, The Book of Will finds an unforgettable 
 true story of love\, loss\, and laughter\, and sheds new light on a man yo
 u may think you know.\n\nTickets $10-$25 online\, by phone\, or at the doo
 r!\n\nFri. 11/6 at 7:30 pm \\(opening night reception after the show!\\)\n
 \nSat. 11/7 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap House - beer\, cider\,
  wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/8 at 2 pm\n\nFri. 11/13 at 10 a
 m \\(Student Matinee\, all welcome!\\)\n\nFri. 11/13 at 7:30 pm \\(ASL Int
 erpretation provided!\\)\n\nSat. 11/14 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English
  Tap House - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/15 a
 t 2 pm\n\nThurs. 11/19 at 7:30 pm \\(Pay-what-you-WILL night!\\)\n\nFri. 1
 1/20 at 7:30 pm\n\nSat. 11/21 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap Hous
 e - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/22 at 2 pm \\
 (closing show!\\)\n\nAbout the producer: Solano College Theatre is dedicat
 ed to providing quality theatre arts education to the next generation of t
 heatre professionals and producing shows that contribute meaningfully to t
 he culture and entertainment of our Solano County community.
LOCATION:Solano Col
URL:http://www.solanocollegetheatre.org/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The MAC FREE November 7-8 with Bank of America Museums on Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T170000
UID:2610239qo5jn_kt0uF-hXipg-Jmw
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is November 7-8. \n\nWith Thanksgiving and winter just around
  the corner\, the late fall season means just one thing: it’s the perfec
 t time for some indoor fun at your local museum!  The “MAC” \\(Napa V
 alley Museum of Art & Culture\\) has exciting exhibits including Eames & E
 ames: Meet the Couple Who Defined Modern Design!\, featuring the boundless
  curiosity of Ray and Charles Eames\, two of the 20th century’s most inf
 luential designers. Eames & Eames explores their iterative\, hands-on\, an
 d human-centered approach. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphics
 \, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundbre
 aking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the breadt
 h of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work ope
 ned doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and u
 nderstanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nBank 
 of America Museums on Us program offers FREE weekend general admission on 
 the first full weekend of every month to Bank of America\, Merrill and Ban
 k of America Private Bank credit and debit cardholders. All you need is yo
 ur Bank of America\, Merrill\, or Bank of America Private Bank card and pi
 cture ID for access. \n\nAdditional participating museums can be found he
 re: https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ner
LOCATION:Napa Valley Museum of Art and Culture
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
