BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:STIMULANT: Art as Remedy for Diseased Culture\, Exhibition and Eve
 nts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T220000
UID:261021BsaywvE-K02xqc33xM8_Pg
DESCRIPTION:In a diseased society with failing systems\, what can we do to
  turn things around? For two weeks a new exhibition from Sonoma County’s
  own Apocalypse Studio\, a father and daughter artist duo\, *STIMULANT: A
 rt as Remedy for Diseased Culture* proposes that art is the antidote and 
 creativity is the countermove. This exhibition explores the inner and oute
 r work of co-creating that antidote: art that stimulates society’s creat
 ivity - the social sculpture we all create together. There will be two per
 formances\, two lectures\, a Parisian -style Art Salon\, and times to visi
 t the large exhibition and talk with the artists. All events are free to 
 attend. Visit www.apocalypse.art/stimulant for details and schedule of eve
 nts.
LOCATION:Laguna Lab
URL:https://apocalypse.art/stimulant/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marin School of the Arts presents Ride the Cyclone (Teen Edition)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T150000
UID:261020qBuscGmZ80qwr_42TAXGKw
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to Ride the Cyclone!\n\nFunny\, wildly original\, un
 expectedly moving\, and just a little bit twisted\, Ride the Cyclone is th
 e cult-hit musical that has become a phenomenon with audiences around the 
 world. When six members of a high school choir meet an untimely end in a r
 oller coaster accident\, they awaken in a strange carnival limbo where a m
 ysterious fortune-telling machine offers them an impossible chance: one of
  them can return to life. To decide who deserves the second chance\, each 
 must tell their story in a bizarre\, hilarious\, and heartfelt competition
  unlike anything you’ve seen before.
LOCATION:Novato High School Center for the Arts
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/marin-school-of-the-art
 s-presents-ride-the-cyclone-teen-edition/19953644/2026-11-07T13
