BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art FREE Nov 7-8 Bank of America Museums o
 n Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T170000
UID:261102jxqvpseliUmSRa_qg2k4Ig
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is November 7-8. \n\nWith Thanksgiving and winter just around
  the corner\, the late fall season means just one thing: it’s the perfec
 t time for some indoor fun at your local museum! The Sonoma Valley Museum 
 of Art has exciting exhibits including brand new installation The Real-Lif
 e Art History of M. Louise Stanley\, an exhibit sponsored by Bank of Ameri
 ca that celebrates a unique Bay Area Figurative artist for her wildly imag
 inative narratives and distinctly female perspective\, shaped by her keen 
 observations of everyday life and setting her apart from her male contempo
 raries. The exhibit features Sanley’s large-scale acrylic paintings\, go
 uache and watercolor works on paper\, sculptural objects\, sketchbooks\, s
 tudies\, photos\, and notes from her personal archives\, showing the artis
 t’s perspective across multiple media forms. \n\nBank of America Museum
 s on Us program offers FREE weekend general admission on the first full we
 ekend of every month to Bank of America\, Merrill and Bank of America Priv
 ate Bank credit and debit cardholders. All you need is your Bank of Americ
 a\, Merrill\, or Bank of America Private Bank card and picture ID for acce
 ss. \n\nAdditional participating museums can be found here: https://about
 .bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-partner
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Museum of Art
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Churros & Soft Pretzels Cooking Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T130000
UID:261031Aby50HIYQki5XCriMnKy8A
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, November 8\, 2026 11:00 am to 1:00 pm\n\nLocation\n\n
 Room 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nCategory\n\nBilingual\, Culinary Arts\n\nExpe
 rience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n5\\+\n\nChildren must be accompanied 
 by an adult.\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$35\n\nGet ready to roll\, twist\, f
 ry\, and bake! In this fun\, hands-on class\, participants will learn how 
 to make two delicious favorites from scratch: traditional Mexican churros 
 and warm\, soft pretzels.We’ll start by preparing the dough and learning
  the proper techniques for shaping and cooking each treat. For the churros
 \, participants will learn how to pipe the dough into the classic ridged s
 hape\, fry them until golden and crispy\, and finish them with cinnamon su
 gar.For the soft pretzels\, we’ll learn how to prepare and shape the dou
 gh into the iconic pretzel twist\, give them their traditional baking-soda
  bath\, and bake them until golden brown with a soft\, chewy center.Along 
 the way\, we’ll share professional tips for working with dough\, control
 ling frying and baking temperatures\, and getting the perfect texture ever
 y time.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/churros-soft-pretzels/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Timely Wisdom
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T190000
UID:261029aFSErweRYky5dN11q8skGQ
DESCRIPTION:The Power of Storytelling in Troubling Times\n\nWe will explor
 e storytelling as a creative way to wield the liberating power of the Dhar
 ma in our daily lives\, especially in these troubling times.  \n\nDrawin
 g on the lifelong commitments of Paula Arai’s research-based writing as 
 a contemplative practice and Kathie Fischer’s focus on Zen practice in d
 omestic and monastic modes\, we will invite people to help us create our o
 wn community story about wielding the compassionate teaching of the Dharma
  in these times.
LOCATION:The Glaser Center
URL:https://events.humanitix.com/https-events-humanitix-com-timely-wisdom-
 2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marin Farmers Markets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T130000
UID:261029VUv3u_daCEmyWCPvCul8Ww
DESCRIPTION:Price: Free Sponsor: Marin Center\n\nExplore the bounty of sum
 mer at the Marin Farmers Markets. Taste vine-ripened tomatoes\, corn that 
 was picked that morning\, and peaches so juicy you have to bend over just 
 to get a bite. Farm-fresh eggs\, grass-fed beef\, artisan c heeses\, raw m
 ilk\, and freshly baked breads complete the shopping exper ience. Specialt
 y prepared foods and handmade art add to the magic of the market. Enjoy th
 e intimate feeling of the Thursday Marin Farmers Market\, an ideal place t
 o meet for lunch and pick up fresh produce for the weekend. Discover the a
 bundance and diversity of product at the celebrated Sunday Marin Farmers M
 arket\, the third largest farmers market in California. Turn your dollar i
 nto a vote for local sustainable agriculture\, shrink your eco-footprint\,
  and revive the feeling of being intimate ly connected to your food by mee
 ting your farmers face-to-face. The market takes place rain or shine.  www
 .aginstitutemarin.org
LOCATION:Marin County Civic Center
URL:https://www.marincounty.org/main/calendar#/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Park Admission for Veterans and Active Military
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T170000
UID:2610282W0P9gO1mkmSS0jPZOZAXQ
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of their service to the United States\, Jack Lo
 ndon State Historic Park will provide free admission to all active-duty mi
 litary and veterans on Nov. 7\, 8\, 9\, 10\, and 11 - Veterans Day – 202
 6.\n\nBlending the fascinating history of one of America’s most prolific
  and successful writers with the serenity of nature\, Jack London State Hi
 storic Park offers more than 29 miles of back-country trails that roam thr
 ough mixed forests\, redwood groves\, oak woodlands\, and grassy meadows i
 n Sonoma County’s Valley of the Moon.  \n\nActive duty or retired mili
 tary identification or form DD214 can be presented at the entry kiosk to r
 eceive free admission.\n\nAdmission\, regularly priced at $15\, covers one
  vehicle of up to nine passengers for the day.  Park hours are 9 a.m. to 
 5 p.m. daily.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Oak Grove Picnic Area (standing
  capacity)
URL:http://www.jacklondonpark.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
