BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Self-Compassion for Shame: Practical Skills for Emotional Wellbein
 g
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T160000
UID:261012S4AhziqYZkedv3gUQvptYQ
DESCRIPTION:with Christopher Germer and Carolina Bautista-Velez\n\nWhat’
 s wrong with you? Who do you think you are?\n\nAll humans can experience s
 hame—including the most practiced meditators and meditation teachers. It
  can even happen when we’re entirely innocent of wrongdoing\, as well as
  when we make a mistake. Whenever we feel bad about ourselves\, for whatev
 er reason\, there’s usually a touch of shame present. It strikes us at t
 he core of our being and yet has nothing to do with who we really are.\n\n
 The power of shame is largely an illusion. As meditation teacher Tara Brac
 h says\, shame often masquerades as a “trance of unworthiness” that ge
 ts its power from our instinctive avoidance of it. However\, when we look 
 at shame through the eyes of self-compassion\, we can discover something q
 uite surprising—that shame is an innocent emotion arising from a univers
 al wish to be loved. This insight opens the door to compassion and self-un
 derstanding. Research shows that self-compassion is the opposite of shame.
  As self-compassion goes up\, shame goes down.\n\nIn this benefit workshop
 \, Chris Germer and Carolina Bautista-Velez present the practice of Self-C
 ompassion for Shame\, specifically tailored to loosen the grip of shame in
  our own lives. The workshop includes short talks\, exercises\, practices\
 , and discussion. Participants will learn 5-6 simple tools to bring home t
 o use in their daily life.\n\nAll are invited to attend this benefit with 
 the awareness that shame can be a difficult human emotion—and that self-
 compassion itself can be emotionally activating. The workshop may be emoti
 onally challenging\, so some familiarity with practicing self-compassion b
 efore joining this workshop may be helpful.\n\nExperienced self-compassion
  teachers will be available as mentors\, in-person and online\, to provide
  information or emotional support to participants\, as needed.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/self-compassion-for-sh
 ame-practical-skills-for-emotional-wellbeing-cr1b26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mark McLay & The Dustdevils In Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T141500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T163000
UID:2610127BHkELU3zka5N6LLz_a4VQ
DESCRIPTION:Mark McLay & The Dustdevils in concert at The Lost Church\, an
  intimate listening space where the audience is close to the performers\, 
 the volume is at a comfortable level\, and there's a bar!\n\nMark McLay & 
 The Dustdevils play original American rock and roll drawing from a song pa
 lette similar to John Hiatt\, Jackson Browne\, and Bruce Springsteen. Mark
 ’s expressive vocals carry tuneful melodies and meaningful lyrics\, wrap
 ped in sophisticated\, song-first arrangements that balance grit\, heart\,
  hope\, and humor.\n\nBacked by The Dustdevils—Dan Ransford:Drums\, Eric
  Straus:Bass\, Mark Harris:Lead Guitar\, Riki Reinking:Harmonies/Blues Har
 p\, Dallis Craft:Keyboards/Harmonies-—the band moves effortlessly from h
 ard-nosed rock to tender\, reflective moments\, always in service of the s
 ong. Praised by critics at KRSH\, KPFA\, and the North Bay Bohemian\, thei
 r honest\, evocative sound has been featured in film\, TV\, and radio—an
 d it’s even better live.\n\nMark will be performing a few songs solo as 
 well!\n\nhttps://www.markmclay.com\n\nLive Video: https://youtu.be/pr2y8pS
 RzkY?si=qRZQqnO5gGpJk4bA
LOCATION:The Lost Church Santa Rosa
URL:https://tinyurl.com/MarkMcLayDustdevilsRosa
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
