BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Upcycled Fashion Club (SUFClub)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T190000
UID:26103127-PgUa9qk2lJIqf06hWGg
DESCRIPTION:Second Tuesday of every Month 5:00 PM – 7:00 PM\n\nThis Sess
 ion\n\nEvent Series \\(See All\\)\n\nTuesday\, November 10\, 2026 5:00 pm 
 to 7:00 pm\n\nEvery second Tuesday\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 201\, Fiber Arts St
 udio\n\nCategory\n\nFiber Arts\, Sustainability\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll
  Levels\n\nAges\n\nGeared towards Young Adults and Teens 14\\+ \\(young at
  heart adults are also welcome!\\)\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\nFree\n\nSonoma
  Upcycled Fashion Club \\(SUFClub\\) is an ongoing club for young adults/t
 eens \\(14\\+\\) and the young at heart who want to make their clothes mor
 e interesting\, more personal\, and way more them. Meet us on the second T
 uesday of every month for an evening of hands-on fashion hacking\, creativ
 e experimentation\, and community. Time to cut\, stitch\, patch\, deconstr
 uct\, reconstruct\, customize\, and completely rethink your project. This 
 is a guided DIY experience so you can work on your own projects\, swap ide
 as\, learn from other makers\, and receive guidance or help from professio
 nal upcycling designer and artist Xochitl of Coyote Creates. The Fiber Art
 s Studio provides a third space in which you have access to irons\, sewing
  machines\, scissors\, and all the textile supplies and tools you need. Al
 l skill levels are welcome. Bring a friend to the club!\n\nwhat to bring\n
 \nBring clothing\, bags\, fabrics\, and accessories you’re bored with\, 
 something you scored at the thrift store\, or a garment that’s been sitt
 ing in the back of your closet waiting for its second chance.\n\nAny speci
 alty materials you’d like to incorporate \\(optional\\)\, such as fabric
 \, buttons\, or sentimental patches\n\nwhat’s included\n\nUse of studio 
 sewing machines\, mending tools\, and basic supplies\n\nThread\, needles\,
  patches\, seam rippers\, and materials\n\nGuidance and support as you wor
 k on your project\n\nA welcoming\, collaborative environment and opportuni
 ty to create a niche community\n\nCost\n\nThis club is free to attend\, bu
 t donations great and small are appreciated. They pay our wonderful Club m
 onitor and help us keep community programming accessible\, including use o
 f studio equipment\, shared tools\, and basic mending materials.\n\nLookin
 g for Something Different?\n\nIf you’re interested in mending and repair
 ing garments rather than creating them\, join our Monthly Mending Bar on t
 he fourth Thursday of each month\, where we repair textile projects and le
 arn practical mending skills. Need more time to work on a project? Our wee
 kly Fiber Arts Happy Hour meets Wednesdays from 4:00 PM –6:00 pm and off
 ers open studio time for independent work on stitching\, mending\, knittin
 g\, crochet\, weaving\, and other fiber arts projects.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/sonoma-upcycled-fashion-clu
 b/2026-11-10/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Park Admission for Veterans and Active Military
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T170000
UID:261028c6BCLsSlgE23dfiJHHTxiQ
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of their service to the United States\, Jack Lo
 ndon State Historic Park will provide free admission to all active-duty mi
 litary and veterans on Nov. 7\, 8\, 9\, 10\, and 11 - Veterans Day – 202
 6.\n\nBlending the fascinating history of one of America’s most prolific
  and successful writers with the serenity of nature\, Jack London State Hi
 storic Park offers more than 29 miles of back-country trails that roam thr
 ough mixed forests\, redwood groves\, oak woodlands\, and grassy meadows i
 n Sonoma County’s Valley of the Moon.  \n\nActive duty or retired mili
 tary identification or form DD214 can be presented at the entry kiosk to r
 eceive free admission.\n\nAdmission\, regularly priced at $15\, covers one
  vehicle of up to nine passengers for the day.  Park hours are 9 a.m. to 
 5 p.m. daily.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Oak Grove Picnic Area (standing
  capacity)
URL:http://www.jacklondonpark.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
