BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shadows of Vallejo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261112T193000
UID:261101OxsqNoWFkEWoUoKEtmwAZQ
DESCRIPTION:What happens when the attorney defending California's most not
 orious killers faces criminal charges himself? This gripping presentation 
 pulls back the curtain on one of Solano County's most enigmatic public def
 enders. Presented by his daughter\, this event offers an unflinching\, ins
 ider look at the chaotic 55-year legal career\, shocking criminal charges\
 , and ultimate redemption of attorney Stephen Camden-the subject of her tr
 ue-crime book\,Camden Files:Did the Ex-Public Defender of Vallejo\, CA Hir
 e Someone to Murder His Ex-Wife's Boyfriend? In the late 1960s and 1970s\,
  Camden's career intersected with the darkest corners of true crime. He re
 gularly interacted with and represented infamous inmates like Charles Mans
 on and Edmund Kemper at Vacaville's California Medical Facility. Yet\, his
  personal life proved just as volatile as his courtroom battles. Widely re
 cognized in his prime as the charismatic "Rod Stewart" of the legal commun
 ity\, this '80s rock-star attorney lived on the edge. His non-conformist l
 ifestyle eventually caught up with him\, leading to a shocking solicitatio
 n of murder charge that stripped him of his role as Vallejo's head public 
 defender. The presentation delivers a raw look at Camden's public career\,
  his personal wreckage\, and his inspiring journey to reinvent himself thr
 ough private practice. Attendees will explore his involvement in several h
 igh-profile murder cases\, his own dramatic trial\, and how local library 
 archives unsealed these hidden historical insights. Ultimately\, it is a p
 owerful story about human resilience and the evolution of modern public de
 fense. A book signing will follow the discussion.
LOCATION:Vallejo John F. Kennedy Library
URL:https://solanolibrary.libnet.info/event/17696791
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
