BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SCOTT CAPURRO is back at Barrel Proof • Friday 11/13 • Downtow
 n Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T220000
UID:261103WsvdlEhPNEyDU4Wq1Qh9Pw
DESCRIPTION:Friday night stand-up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa with SCOTT
  CAPURRO!\n\nStand-up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nVIP TABLES NOW AVAI
 LABLE! Snag a table for 4 with preferred seating\, your own private call b
 utton to summon service\, and your first round of beer/cider (or a bottle 
 of wine) for only $105! Every Friday night hilarious comedians from The Ba
 y Area and beyond perform at Barrel Proof Lounge. Stick around after for l
 ate-night karaoke!\n\nFresh lineup of funny each Friday.\n\nThis Week: Hos
 t: Josh Argyle Nate Schwartz\n\nHeadliner: Scott Capurro\n\nScott Capurro 
 was reared in San Francisco. At age 3\, he swam the English Channel. Since
  1993\, he’s avoided AIDS by telling unsavory jokes in every English spe
 aking country. Scott is trusting and thus surrounded by duplicity\, yet he
  continues challenging himself\, because he’s physically challenged and 
 emotionally unavailable\, aka married.\n\nDescribed by San Francisco Weekl
 y (free press\, edited by lesbians and designed by trannys with large hand
 s and hidden agendas) as “stand-up in the very best possible sense – d
 eadpan\, ever-alert and hilarious”.\n\nScott has appeared in Mrs. Doubtf
 ire\, where\, effortlessly\, he played a homosexual\; and Star Wars: Phant
 om Menace\, where\, breathlessly\, he wore a body stocking. A gay designer
  who sports two heads might’ve been a predictable sequel\; instead Scott
  waddled off to the UK\, in search of a compassionate\, creative culture.\
 n\nDisappointed and slightly bloated\, Scott spends hours each day playing
  classical piano\, conversing in French and managing his meds. He knows (w
 ink\, wink) several death row inmates and George Clooney. Well\, he met Ge
 orge once. They’re both vegetarians. Actually\, Scott is. Clooney said h
 e was\, to impress Scott. Guys on death row eat anything.\n\n21+ Doors - 7
 p / Show - 8p $20adv / $25door\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** 
 for all sorts of good times ahead.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/scott-capurro-is-back-at-barrel-proof-fri
 day-1113-downtown-santa-rosa-tickets-2001396608131?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Mirror: Stage Play
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T190000
UID:2611034kwR8fntWEuaIuIEsQCd2A
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for an unforgettable evening of drama and excitement
  with The Mirror Stage play. The Mirror is a one-man play that takes you i
 nside the mind of James\, a man caught between his present and past selves
 . In a series of intimate conversations with his reflection\, James confro
 nts his inner self\, the protective voice that has shielded him from pain\
 , rejection\, and vulnerability throughout his life. But James wants more.
  He wants to live openly\, to take risks\, to love & feel deeply\, even if
  it means getting hurt. His inner self resists\, clinging to the walls he'
 s built around himself. Through their dialogue\, they explore relationship
 s that never quite worked\, career choices driven by fear rather than pass
 ion and commitment\, and the triggers and traumas that shaped James.
LOCATION:Sir Winston Event House
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/the-mirror-stage-play-tickets-20006613960
 92
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
