DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T190000
UID:261016SHyx6VWLuUSUZnN8XuTpWQ
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Andaz Napa - A Concept By Hyatt
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108590341?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening with Zoë Lewis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T210000
UID:2610163jEGLb-zj0K6jS13OkwSPQ
DESCRIPTION:Affectionately know as “a band in a body\,” Zoë Lewis pla
 ys vintage jazz and world beat grooves on anything from the piano to ukul
 ele to the spoons! \n\nOriginally from the UK\, this astonishing singer-s
 ongwriter has called Provincetown her home for the last 32 years. She's tr
 aveled to over 70 countries picking up musical grooves and stories along t
 he way\, released ten albums of original material\, toured with the Indigo
  Girls\, Judy Collins\, Richie Havens\, Nanci Griffiths and has even opene
 d for Pat Benatar on the ukulele! \n\nHer songs have won numerous accolad
 es\, have appeared in films\, on Broadway\, in commercials\, and most rece
 ntly on the Netflix kid show *StoryBots*. She’s written 3 musicals that 
 received rave reviews\, performs for OLIVIA cruises\, and takes her show t
 o Puerto Vallarta\, Mexico every winter.\n\nZoe will be joined by the fabu
 lous KATE WOLF on bass.\n\nAn evening with Zoe Lewis will leave you with l
 ong-lasting joy. Join us!
LOCATION:Congregation Ner Shalom
URL:https://www.nershalom.org/event-calendar/2026/11/14-zoe-lewis
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
