SUMMARY:Archery Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T130000
UID:261031LMw7_Oq8qUm8iu4i4gnBgA
DESCRIPTION:Come learn the basics of archery from safety to form in a fun\
 , outdoor environment. Our certified instructors will help you develop you
 r skills and confidence on the range. This basic class is appropriate for 
 beginners as well as those who haven't picked up the bow in a while. ***Ch
 ildren under 13 must attend with an adult.***\n\nTuition: $50\\* **Use Cod
 e: PACSUN10 to receive $10 off!** (not to be combined with any other offer
 )\n\n\\*When you become a Vilda Member\, you and a friend can attend all o
 ur year-round family classes for free! Memberships also make great gifts!!
  Learn more at https://www.vildanature.org/vilda-membership\n\nArchery Bas
 ics is part of Vilda\, which is dedicated to facilitating meaningful conne
 ctions with the natural world. Vilda started in Fairfax\, California in 20
 08 and has been running programs since then\, now serving over 2000 kids a
  year in Marin\, Sonoma\, and Tahoe. The organization is a 501c(3) non-pro
 fit led by founder Mia Andler\, offering nature education\, youth programs
 \, homeschool programs\, and summer camps in several Bay Area communities 
 and in Tahoe and Truckee. Vilda recently won the prestigious Pacific Sun 2
 026 Award for "Best Summer Camp"!
LOCATION:Stafford Lake Park
URL:https://vilda.squarespace.com/family-adult#archerynov15
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Start your family tree: Discover your family's story
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T160000
UID:261027jdaiJnRa0U2SUQJglxKiOw
DESCRIPTION:This free talk and hands-on session will enable you to:\n\n- B
 uild a family tree in minutes\n\n- Search census and military records\n\n-
  Find birth\, marriage and death records\n\n- Explore historic newspapers\
 n\n- Trace your ancestry back hundreds of years\n\nYou will leave the sess
 ion with your family tree started! This event is presented by Michael Von 
 der Porten\, a sixth-generation Sonoma County resident\, historian\, resea
 rcher\, author\, and tour guide. This is a project from the Western Sonoma
  County Historical Society. It will be preceded by an update by the Histor
 ical Society\, including the latest about the West County Museum and the L
 uther Burbank Experiment Farm.\n\nWhat to Bring:\n\n- Full name of a paren
 t\, grandparent\, or earlier ancestor\n\n- Birth date\n\n- Death date \\(i
 f applicable\\)\n\n- Place of birth \n\nNote: We'll begin with deceased f
 amily members for privacy reasons.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:http://Www.wschs.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
