BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jim Lauderdale
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
UID:261020kBWWUaoHz0W9mh3CxXJ0pw
DESCRIPTION:Two-time Grammy-winning singer and master songwriter Jim Laude
 rdale is both a "songwriter's songwriter\," who's written/co-written many 
 modern classics for iconic artists\, as well as an intuitive sideman\, who
 's enhanced the music of a bevy of esteemed musicians. As a solo artist\, 
 since 1986 up until now\, he's created a bodywork spanning 37 albums of im
 aginative roots music\, encompassing all that is today’s musical landsca
 pe. His combination of Country\, Bluegrass\, Soul\, R&B and Rock has helpe
 d to pave the way for the current Americana movement.\n\nFor several decad
 es\, Jim has written songs for and worked with some of the finest artists 
 in traditional and modern music including Ralph Stanley\, Elvis Costello\,
  George Strait\, Buddy Miller\, Lucinda Williams\, John Oates\, Solomon Bu
 rke\, Lee Ann Womack\, Old Crow Medicine Show\, Mary Chapin Carpenter\, Bl
 ake Shelton\, the Dixie Chicks\, Vince Gill\, Patty Loveless\, and Gary Al
 lan among others.\n\nLauderdale co-hosts "The Buddy & Jim Show" weekly rad
 io program on SiriusXM with Buddy Miller. Recently\, the Americana Music A
 ssociation honoured him with the WagonMaster Lifetime Achievement Award. J
 im has certainly earned it\, having released a staggering 37 albums with t
 he latest My Favorite Place out June 21st on Sky Crunch Records 2024. \n\n
 Whether solo or band\, Jim Lauderdale a triple threat performer\, songwrit
 er and musician who is constantly reinventing himself!
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern Novato
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108940639?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author's Afternoon with Marlo Faulkner on "The Second Mrs. London"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T153000
UID:2610193g6Gr-7JzU6pD47uZfdh-Q
DESCRIPTION:Step into the world of Charmian Kittredge London with author M
 arlo Faulkner as she presents her book\, “The Second Mrs. London."\n\nA 
 native of Coeur d’Alene\, Idaho\, Marlo Faulkner has led a remarkable an
 d adventurous life\, working as a roadie\, English instructor\, columnist\
 , literary scholar\, and a featured speaker for the Jack London Society. H
 er fascination with Charmian London began during a visit to Jack London St
 ate Historic Park\, where she discovered Charmian’s private apartment. Y
 ears of research\, travel\, and study culminated in her new novel\, “The
  Second Mrs. London\,” bringing to life the extraordinary story of one o
 f Sonoma Valley’s most captivating women.\n\nSet in San Francisco at the
  turn of the 20th century\, the novel tells the story of Charmian\, a bold
  and ambitious woman whose life is forever changed when she meets young wr
 iter Jack London. From a broken picnic date to a devoted partnership as fr
 iend\, confidante\, editor\, and companion. Their story is one of passion\
 , resilience\, and determination.\n\nFaulkner will share details of the re
 markable life of Charmian London\, read excerpts from her book inspired by
  this extraordinary woman\, and sign copies for attendees.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/the-second-mrs-london-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yototl de Healdsburg 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:261017a1Gai1Js5km4IxZ4r8N_rw
DESCRIPTION:Ballet Folklórico Comunitario Yolotl brings a captivating dis
 play of bright costumes\, swirling skirts\, and cultural comunitario to th
 e Raven Theater!\n\n“Yolotl“ means ”heart“ in Nahuatl. The languag
 e\, which is part of a group of languages in the Uto-Aztecan language fami
 ly\, is spoken by millions of people in central Mexico and in smaller popu
 lations in the United States. Experience the heart of Mexico and it’s ma
 ny regions and cultures with the beauty of Ballet Folklórico Comunitario 
 Yolotl\, a cadre of about 55 dancers formed under the direction of “maes
 tra” Yolanda Girón.\n\nSunday\, Nov. 15th\, at 5:00 PM. Doors open 4:00
  PM.
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/yolotl-de-healdsburg/?eventstart=17947
 90800&eventend=1794798000&timezone=America%2FLos_Angeles
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Endless Inspiration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T180000
UID:261014jJGpmpkbgU2DMp4xculJOg
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  10/12/26\n\n**NOVEMBER EXHIBIT: 
 ENDLESS INSPIRATION**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES **– October 26  – November 22\
 , 2026**\n\n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, November 7\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to
  meet Ron Sumner and Karen Miller and learn about their art and inspiratio
 n.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a 
 beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSo
 noma County artist\, **Ron Sumner\,** presents **Endless Inspiration**\, a
  collection of new paintings and classic works that highlight his lifelong
  love of nature featuring landscapes\, animals and wildlife\, with a speci
 al focus on birds.  The essence of this golden state shines forth in “C
 alifornia Hills\,” a large oil painting of a sweep of oak covered hills.
    Turning to wildlife\, Sumner’s masterful watercolor rendition in th
 e “Young Fox” captures its wild nature on stark alert.  And the compe
 lling presence of a most majestic bird is beautifully memorialized in his 
 “Blue Heron” watercolor.  Other birds depicted in his works include p
 arrots\, penguins and owls.  “In my painting\, I always strive to trans
 late my emotional response to the world of nature around us – to share t
 his deep feeling with those who view my work\,” commented Sumner on his 
 inspiration.\n\nA lifelong Northern Californian\, Sumner began his art tra
 ining in school.  After earning a BFA from the California College of Arts
  & Crafts\, he was a technical illustrator for a number of years before tr
 ansitioning to a full-time fine arts painter.  With an emphasis in waterc
 olor\, he has won numerous awards\, including Best of Show at the Society 
 of Western Artists.  His portrait of John F. Kennedy is part of the perma
 nent collection at the John F. Kennedy Library.  He has exhibited widely 
 and was part of the Veterans Art Show for CA vets in 2023.\n\nMeet the art
 ist: Sumner will co-host Art Nite on 11/5 from 5 pm to 7 pm.\n\nThe Stairw
 ay Smallworks Showcase features **Karen Miller’**s **Historic Gems\,** f
 eaturing pastel paintings that honor our history – local artifacts that 
 are disappearing.  Highlighting this exhibit\, “Ghost Bridge\,” an ea
 rly 20th century railroad bridge known as Healdsburg Railroad Bridge is so
 on to give way for the Smart Train.  Its unique style is a key element to
  our local character but sadly could not be upgraded for modern rail.  Fr
 om old trucks to a beloved schoolhouse\, these paintings harken fond memor
 ies.  Part of our world for years\, they enriched our lives and are not t
 o be forgotten.  Noted Miller on the impetus for her series\, “I want t
 o catch old things before they’re gone – memorializing those things cl
 ose to our hearts.”\n\nMeet the artist: Miller will host the Gallery on 
 October 26 and November 2\, 11\, 14 & 15 from 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\n Also j
 oin us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, November 5\, 5 – 7 pm. 
  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a communi
 ty event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participati
 ng.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\,
  Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    
 **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beve
 rly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
