BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Senderos & Rutas y Aventuras: Retos en las montañas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
UID:260930i1JRZkoLPUO-SZKE5dKkPA
DESCRIPTION:\\[Translated to English Below\\] Este otoño\, acompaña a gu
 ías de Jack London Park Partners y Sonoma Ecology Center en una series de
  caminatas de nivel intermediario que intercambiarán entre Jack London St
 ate Historic Park y Sugarloaf Ridge State Park. Las excursiones serán pri
 mariamente los sábados 10\, 17\, y 24 de octubre\, el 7 y 21 de noviembre
 \, y el domingo 15 de noviembre\, y cada una aumentará en dificultad o du
 ración\, por la cual no son apropiadas para niños menores de 12 años.\n
 \nEvento gratuito\; requiere registración. Hay transportación disponible
  gratuita dentro de un radio de 20 millas al parque para familias que la n
 ecesiten. Para detalles y registración\, visita https://sec.regfox.com/re
 to2026 \n\nAlternativamente\, llama a (Carlos: 707-938-5216\, ext 9\; Mar
 io 707-387-4087\; Alma 707-247-5767)\, entre martes y sábado) o escríben
 os a senderos@sonomaecologycenter.org. ¿No puedes acompañarnos para este
  evento? ¡Guarda la fecha el 11 de octubre para más aventuras!\n\nSender
 os Naturales es parcialmente respaldado por una beca de Parks California.\
 n\nFotografía cortesía de Alma Shaw\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nEnglish: This fall\, join Jack London Park 
 Partners and Sonoma Ecology Center staff in a 6-week series of intermediat
 e hikes between Jack London State Historic Park and Sugarloaf Ridge State 
 Park. The hikes will be primarily on Saturdays\, October 10\, 17\, and 24\
 , and November 7 and 21\, with the exception of Sunday\, November 15\, and
  they will switch parks back and forth. Each hike will increase in length 
 or difficulty\, which does not make this series appropriate for children u
 nder 12 years old. \n\nThis event is planned around a primarily Latino au
 dience\, but all are welcome to this bilingual hiking series.\n\nFamilies 
 from underrepresented groups are welcome to join. Free transportation avai
 lable within a 20 mile radius of the park for families in need. For questi
 ons\, please email senderos@sonomaecologycenter.org.\n\nThis event is part
 ially supported by Route to Parks\, a project of Parks California.\n\nPhot
 o Courtesy of Alma Shaw
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Beauty Ranch Meadow\, Sugarloaf
  Ridge State Park\, Kenwood\, CA
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/reto2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Veterans Holiday Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
UID:260930cqiS-yivFUq6ErM_n0Pnsw
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma VFW Auxiliary Post 1943 will host its 4th Annual Ve
 terans Holiday Market on Saturday\, November 14\, from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m.\,
  and Sunday\, November 15\, from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m. at the Veterans Memoria
 l Building\, 126 First St. West\, Sonoma.\n\nThe two-day holiday market wi
 ll feature one-of-a-kind\, limited-edition goods handcrafted by local arti
 sts and makers. With several vendors participating\, shoppers will have an
  opportunity to find unique gifts while supporting the Auxiliary’s missi
 on of helping those who have served and their loved ones.\n\nThe Native Da
 ughters of the Golden West\, Sonoma Parlor No. 209\, will also host a spec
 ial community activity\, “Make a Veteran a Christmas Card.” Community 
 members of all ages are invited to create handmade holiday cards that will
  be delivered to area veterans living in assisted living facilities and nu
 rsing homes.\n\nThe Veterans Holiday Market is free and open to the public
 \, with a special invitation extended to military members\, veterans and t
 heir families. Proceeds from the event will help provide assistance to vet
 erans and military families who are experiencing hardship.\n\nThe VFW Auxi
 liary is an all-volunteer service organization whose members include the s
 pouses\, parents\, grandparents\, brothers\, sisters and other family memb
 ers of those who have served in overseas combat. Since 1934\, members of S
 onoma VFW Auxiliary Post 1943 have worked to support those who have served
  and strengthen the community around them.\n\nThe Auxiliary’s community 
 service efforts have included toy and monetary donations to Toys for Tots\
 , Christmas gifts and cards for veterans at the Yountville Veterans Home\,
  as well as clothing and food drives benefiting local emergency service or
 ganizations.\n\nThe Veterans Holiday Market is an opportunity for the enti
 re community to come together during the holiday season—not only to shop
  and celebrate\, but also to show appreciation for those who have served a
 nd to remind veterans and their loved ones that they are valued\, remember
 ed and not alone.\n\nVeteran Families Helping Veterans\n\nFor more informa
 tion contact: Debbie Chandler \\(707\\)364-2734
LOCATION:Sonoma Veterans Building
URL:http://vfwpost1943.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Echoes of Innocence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:260929Wyt5xEh-RkyF6A_4wGBuAg
DESCRIPTION:Echoes of Innocence\n\nNovember 14\, 15 & 16\, 2026\n\nWeill H
 all\, Green Music Center\n\n**Francesco Lecce-Chong\,** conductor\n\n**Oli
 ver Herbert\,** cello\n\n**Elisa Sunshine\,** soprano\n\n**SERGEI RACHMANI
 NOFF:** *Vocalise* in E minor for Soprano and Orchestra\, Opus 34\, No. 14
  **CAMILLE SAINT-SAËNS:** Concerto No. 1 in A minor for Cello and Orchest
 ra\, Opus 33 **GUSTAV MAHLER:** Symphony No. 4 in G major for Soprano and 
 Orchestra\n\nRachmaninoff’s *Vocalise* is a landmark piece of wordless l
 onging and quiet intensity. Bay Area native Oliver Herbert performs Saint-
 Saëns’ Cello Concerto No. 1\, a work that unfolds in a single continuou
 s movement\, shifting seamlessly between urgency and repose. Closing the p
 erformance\, Mahler’s ethereal Symphony No. 4 features a soprano in its 
 final movement\, which delivers a radiant and transcendent ending.\n\n**Pr
 ograms\, artists\, dates\, and prices are subject to change without notice
 . Tickets are subject to availability. All Tickets are nonrefundable.**\n\
 nPhoto by Todd Rosenberg
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/echoes-of-innocence/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sunday Sessions in The Lounge – DJs\, Dancing & Requests
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T230000
UID:260929K-duB_qds0apA090_Q-Mng
DESCRIPTION:SUNDAY SESSIONS IN THE LOUNGE ROTATING DJs • OPEN FORMAT •
  REQUESTS WELCOME • NO COVER\n\nSunday nights have a new home in The Lou
 nge at Barrel Proof.\n\nEvery Sunday at 8 PM\, a rotating lineup of DJs ta
 kes over the front room for Sunday Sessions — an open-format dance party
  where the playlist isn't locked into one genre and requests are part of t
 he fun.\n\nOpen format means the DJ gets to read the room. One song might 
 take you back\, the next might be something you were blasting in the car t
 his week. Different genres\, different eras and different DJs from week to
  week\, with plenty of room for the crowd to help steer the night.\n\nGot 
 a song you want to hear? Ask the DJ.\n\nAnd there's more happening under t
 he same roof. Start your evening with Sunday Funday Comedy at 6 PM\, then 
 at 8 PM Barrel Proof gives you two ways to keep the night going:\n\n THE 
 LOUNGE — 8 PM Sunday Sessions Rotating DJs • Open Format • Requests 
 • Dancing\n\n MAIN ROOM — 8 PM Sunday Night Karaoke Grab the mic and 
 sing on the big stage.\n\nDance in the Lounge\, sing in the Main Room\, or
  bounce between the two all night.\n\nEvery Sunday • 8 PM Barrel Proof L
 ounge 501 Mendocino Ave • Downtown Santa Rosa 21+ • No Cover\n\nCheck 
 out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/sunday-sessions-in-the-lounge-djs-dancing
 -requests-tickets-2002178174818?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
