BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trio da Paz
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T173000
UID:260819-1tr2FIfjUmv_sybRdqKhg
DESCRIPTION:Grammy-nominated Trio da Paz\, one of the most visible Brazili
 an jazz groups in the world featuring three of Brazil's most-in-demand mus
 icians: Romero Lubambo on guitar\, Nilson Matta on bass and Duduka da Fons
 eca on drums and percussion. They formed in 1986 and will be celebrating t
 heir 40th anniversary at THE 222 in an exclusive West Coast appearance. To
 gether\, Trio da Paz performs with a strong sense of cohesion\, bringing e
 nergy\, imagination\, and a deep musical connection to their work. The res
 ult is a trio that continues to create distinctive\, personal music\, blen
 ding Brazilian traditions with elements of modern jazz. Trio da Paz's soun
 d reflects a thoughtful integration of Brazilian musical styles and jazz i
 mprovisation\, drawing on the harmonies of bossa nova\, the rhythms of sam
 ba\, and the melodic intricacy of choro. Their acoustic trio format-guitar
 \, bass\, and drums-allows for close interaction among the musicians\, fos
 tering a conversational approach that highlights both rhythmic interplay a
 nd harmonic nuance. While grounded in tradition\, the group approaches fam
 iliar forms with flexibility\, allowing the music to evolve in unexpected 
 but natural directions. Each member\, established on the New York jazz sce
 ne as both a leader and collaborator\, contributes to a collective identit
 y shaped by original compositions alongside interpretations of Brazilian r
 epertoire.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/trio-da-paz/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
