BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CNPS Speaker Series - Author of Indigenous cooking/culture book
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T210000
UID:261104_eaSl8PlsU66iUCQ6wF-1A
DESCRIPTION:Sara Calvosa Olson (Karuk) is the author of *Chími Nu’am: N
 ative California Foodways for the Contemporary Kitchen* (Heyday\, 2023). H
 er work dwells at the intersection of storytelling\, Indigenous food syste
 ms\, traditional phenological knowledge\, and community food security. Wit
 h an interest in using both culturally sound and faithfully updated techni
 ques that honor traditional plants and animals\, her cooking inspires a ne
 w look at California's oldest foods.\n\nJoin Sara in conversation about th
 e past\, present\, and future of food sovereignty\, and how we can develop
  deeper understandings of climate issues by centering Indigenous rematriat
 ion efforts.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Art and Garden Center
URL:https://chapters.cnps.org/milobaker/2026/10/27/november-17-speaker-ser
 ies-sara-calvosa-olson-karuk/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
