BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T170000
UID:261106K4V1JOeZv02KC7tvVtKSOQ
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Montagne Russe Winery and Record Lounge
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108869311?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marin County Arts & Crafts Fair
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T160000
UID:261104gz9bSFQNG0ur8-VUMYpGJw
DESCRIPTION:Have fun\, enjoy music\, and discover handmade treasures! The 
 Marin County Employee Arts & Crafts Fair returns November 18–19\, from 1
 1 a.m.–4 p.m.\, at the Marin Civic Center cafeteria\, Room 237\, in San 
 Rafael.\n\nShop handcrafts and original art while listening to the County 
 Crows employee band. Different vendors and music each day--visit twice!\n\
 nCraving something sweet? The HR & Friends Bake charity sale and individua
 l bakers sell treats on Wednesday only.\n\nCelebrating its 26th anniversar
 y\, this staff-founded tradition is open to the public. Employees particip
 ate on their own time\, and volunteers in the county's MarinShares program
  provide support. \n\nBrowse original paintings\, drawings\, woodcuts\, a
 nd photographs. Crafts include ceramics\, jewelry\, paper art\, potted pla
 nts\, crocheted dolls\, notecards\, candles\, knitted and crocheted wearab
 les\, and lots more.
LOCATION:Marin County Employee Arts & Crafts Fair
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/marin-county-arts-craft
 s-fair/20282610/2026-11-19T11
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Camden Files - book  launch and signing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T210000
UID:261103ptm2EzF960qKC8xlytE1FQ
DESCRIPTION:The Camden Files book launch tour is underway! Join author Can
 dice Camden at these upcoming local events for book presentations & exclus
 ive signings.\n\nThis gripping legal thriller chronicles the 55-year caree
 r of a legendary defense attorney\, Stephen Camden\, as he navigates som
 e of the darkest intersections of California’s justice system. From repr
 esenting high-profile murderers and notorious inmates\, like Charles Manso
 n\, to surviving his own public brush with the law. It is the story of a
  man who spent a lifetime defending the indefensible.\n\nEVENT 1: Book Pre
 sentation & Signing\n\nWhen: Thursday\, November 12th | 6:00 PM – 7:30 P
 M\n\nWhere: Vallejo John F. Kennedy Library \\(Joseph Room\\) — 505 Sant
 a Clara St\, Vallejo\n\nWhat: Pull back the curtain on one of Solano Count
 y’s most enigmatic legal figures. Sponsored by the Vallejo JFK Library.\
 n\nEVENT 2: Chris’ Club Book Party & Signing\n\nWhen: Thursday\, Novembe
