  419 Georgia Street\, \\(at the back of the breezeway\\)\, Third Thursdays
 \, 7–8pm. Donation-based. Wheelchair accessible. Please bring a friend &
  please arrive fragrance free. Masks optional & let us know access needs. 
 Inspired by Theravada lineage and @ebmc\\_oakland\, which was started for 
 and by LGBTQIA\\+ and BIPOC folks to have a space in downtown Oakland that
  centers radical inclusivity. With gratitude for the teachings of Larry Ya
 ng and many other EBMC dharma teachers\, we will read from his book Awaken
 ing Together and similar teachings to create beloved community close to ho
 me.
