SUMMARY:Pendant Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T140000
UID:261106nMuwa2KoyUyQNe8pruZsmg
DESCRIPTION:In this class\, students will learn the art of weaving in a ci
 rcular pattern to create beautiful round pendants. Students will use raffi
 a or a large assortment of strings to create these woven spirals.\n\nYou w
 ill learn how to add columns\, change colors\, and finish your project in 
 this 4 hour workshop.\n\nAll materials will be provided.\n\nThese spirals 
 can be utilized as a wall piece\, or worn as a pendant!\n\nAbout the Teach
 er: Carrie Botto is a self taught multi medium weaver. She started weaving
  with beads over 40 years ago and continues to add skills and techniques t
 o her “tool box”. Carrie travels all over the country now teach severa
 l different classes\, and has taught at Mendocino Art Center\, New Mexico 
 Bead Trader\, Moab Art Center\, and Fiber on 4th in New Mexico. Follow Car
 rie on Instagram @beanstreetstudio!
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/pendant-workshop
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
