DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
UID:261106aTxePpIqBUiFaxK5ewdidA
DESCRIPTION:Riding high from their recent performance at **Hardly Strictl
 y Bluegrass**\, Ameri-Cali Soul band **Wreckless Strangers** are kicking
  off the holiday season with their first Christmas song\, “**Christmas 
 Tears**\,” arriving November 6. The band will debut the single live\, a
 longside its signature blend of originals and crowd-pleasing covers\, at 
 **Rancho Nicasio** on **Friday\, November 20**\, followed by a show at 
 **Lucca Bar & Grill** in **Benicia** on **Saturday\, December 19**.\n\nT
 he two performances bring Wreckless Strangers’ soulful\, roots-driven ro
 ck to two special corners of the Bay Area. On November 20\, the band takes
  the stage at **Rancho Nicasio**\, the historic West Marin roadhouse know
 n for live music\, dinner shows\, and its laid-back country setting. On De
 cember 19\, they perform at **Lucca Bar & Grill** in Benicia\, a waterfr
 ont town with a welcoming small-town feel and a lively dining and music sc
 ene.\n\nOriginally released by **Sonny Thompson and Robert Wilson** and 
 made famous by blues legend **Freddie King**\, “**Christmas Tears**” 
 takes on new life through Wreckless Strangers’ soul-driven arrangement\,
  old-school piano\, and emotionally charged vocals.\n\nRecorded at the leg
 endary **FAME Recording Studios in Muscle Shoals\, Alabama**\, the single
  offers a different perspective on the season. Rather than focusing on the
  usual joy and nostalgia\, the band leans into a more melancholy side of t
 he holidays\, with lead vocalist **Amber Morris** delivering a standout 
 performance that balances technical precision with the song’s raw emotio
 n.\n\nThe idea for the band’s first Christmas release had been circulati
 ng for years. In April\, while visiting Tennessee\, the band found a break
  between shows in Nashville and Knoxville and seized the opportunity to re
 cord at FAME Studios with producer **David Kalmusky\,** whose credits in
 clude Keith Urban\, Carrie Underwood\, Justin Bieber\, and Journey. It was
  Amber who suggested “Christmas Tears\,” an unconventional choice that
  proved to be the perfect fit.\n\n“Christmas Tears” will be available 
 on all streaming platforms on November 6.
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio
URL:http://ranchonicasio.com/events/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Olio Nuovo Harvest and Milling Experience at Gold Ridge Organic Fa
 rms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T141500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T153000
UID:261104hxWhxzxIlEKiDidqkKwSKw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an unforgettable behind-the-scenes journey into th
 e heart of our olive harvest season. This experience offers a rare opportu
 nity to see how our award-winning olive oil is crafted\, from the branches
  of our olive trees to the first drops of the season’s oil.\n\nYour jour
 ney begins with a guided tour of our 88-acre organic farm. You’ll step i
 nto the orchards to watch our expert team harvest fresh olives straight fr
 om the trees at their peak of flavor.\n\nNext\, you’ll visit our state-o
 f-the-art olive oil mill\, where you’ll learn about the milling process 
 and see the olives pressed into vibrant\, fresh Olio Nuovo\, the celebrate
 d “new oil” prized by culinary enthusiasts for its brilliant green hue
  and robust\, peppery finish.\n\nThe highlight comes right at the source: 
 tasting fresh Olio Nuovo straight from the mill just moments after the oli
 ves are crushed.\n\nBook now to secure your spot for this rare\, behind-th
 e-scenes look at our harvest traditions.\n\nImportant Notes: Please wear c
 omfortable shoes suitable for walking on a working farm This outdoor exper
 ience may be canceled due to wet weather. Full refund available.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/627571/olio
 -nuovo-harvest-and-milling-experience
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
