BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stone Wrapping Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T150000
UID:261106pX_D7msS20-X_SbajIZq1Q
DESCRIPTION:In this class\, students will be creating decorative stones\, 
 utilizing wrapping techniques that can be applied outside of this class. S
 tudents will learn 3 basic knots with time allotted between each lesson fo
 r students to experiment creating new stones with the new knot. This appro
 ach allows everyone’s imagination to run wild\, fostering creativity and
  allowing time for new ideas.\n\nAll materials provided.\n\nStudents often
  make 6-8 stones per class.\n\nThere will be discussion breaks\, and a lun
 ch break throughout the class. Please bring water and a paper bag lunch.\n
 \nAbout the Teacher: Carrie Botto is a self taught multi-medium weaver. Sh
 e started weaving with beads over 40 years ago and continues to add skills
  and techniques to her “tool box”. Carrie travels all over the country
  now teaching several different classes\, and has taught at Mendocino Art 
 Center\, New Mexico Bead Trader\, Moab Art Center\, and Fiber on 4th in Ne
 w Mexico. Follow Carrie on Instagram @beanstreetsudio!
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/stone-wrapping
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
