DESCRIPTION:Redwood Writers 2026 Holiday Book & Craft Fair\n\nNovember 21\
 , 2026\, 11 a.m. Finley Center in Santa Rosa FREE!\n\nJoin us on Saturday\
 , November 21\, from 11 a.m. to 1:30 p.m. in Room 5 \\(Senior Wing\\) at t
 he Finley Center for our 3rd Annual Holiday Party and Book & Craft Fair! T
 his lively\, event brings together local authors and crafters\, offering b
 ooks and handmade treasures that make perfect holiday gifts for yourself o
 r your loved ones. Admission is FREE so that you can find the perfect loca
 l gift for your loved ones. The afternoon will be a celebration among frie
 nds\, delicious food\, and creative gifts made by local artisans and autho
 rs.\n\nMembers\, please bring a savory or sweet dish to share for our potl
 uck\, if you can!\n\nMark your calendars and plan to join us for a joyful 
 afternoon of shopping\, mingling\, and celebrating creativity in our commu
 nity.\n\nA chance to meet nice people with cool crafts\, books\, and other
  helpful services for creative souls and writers:\n\nMalena Eljumaily \\(C
 rafts\\): Knitted and crocheted items\, plus other handcrafts\n\nTaylor Me
 tzler \\(Books & Crafts\\): Books\, chainmaille jewelry\, crocheted items\
 n\nPamela Heck \\(Books & Art\\)\n\nRedwood Writers \\(Books\\): Redwood W
 riters anthologies and swag\n\nPatricia L. Morin \\(Books\\): Psychologica
 l paranormal thriller Moloch and the Angel\; short story collections Myste
 ry Montage\, Crime Montage\, Confetti\, Deadly Illusions\n\nStacey Dennick
  \\(Other\\): Comic zines\, plus info on SRJC’s free Lifelong Learning c
 lasses\n\nCrissi Langwell \\(Books & Art\\): Romance books and art\n\nShaw
 n Langwell \\(Books and Marketing Consulting\\): Personal growth and inspi
 rational books helping authors move past the mental obstacles of putting t
 heir work into the world\n\nN.E. White \\(Books\\): Mapmaker Books 1–3\;
  The Legend of Damndrake and The Rescue of Damndrake \\(epic fantasy with 
 dragons\\)\n\nJanet Henker \\(Books\\): Two novels and an anthology\, plus
  baked goods\n\nLaura McHale Holland \\(Books\\): Novels\, short story col
 lections\, memoirs\n\nSarah Paris \\(Books\\): Haiku and magic realism nov
 ellas\n\nNatalie Gould \\(Books\\): Memoir\, plus crafts \\(dried flower w
 reaths\, paintings\, cards\\)\n\nLisa Manterfield \\(Books\\): Mystery/sus
 pense novels A Strange Companion\, The Smallest Thing\, All Our Lies Are T
 rue\n\nDawn Dolan \\(Books\\): Two children’s books with matching merch 
 \\(mugs\, thermoses\, plushies\\)\n\nKen Berman \\(Books\\): Books\, magne
 ts\, and character merch\n\nBrian Martens \\(Books & Art\\): Poetry books 
 Three Raven Gate and Merlin’s Wing\, plus small paintings\n\nNeil Burgst
 ahler \\(Books\\)\n\nJoan Tabb \\(Books\\)\n\nTessa Burns \\(Books\\)
