DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T120000
UID:260820eOkbU6_F7ECSvzDFPMdtrQ
DESCRIPTION:Orchids are the largest family of flowering plants in the worl
 d\, with over 25\,000 species found in nature\, and probably in the order 
 of 150\,000 different hybrids. Many think orchids are difficult to grow\, 
 but with some basic information\, anyone can be successful with growing or
 chids. This presentation will cover: Understanding the basic needs and car
 e for growing most orchids at home. An introduction to the more common orc
 hid groups that are possible to grow. Learning which types can grow outsid
 e on the Sonoma Coast. Registration Encouraged: Visit Upcoming Events to c
 omplete your registration. After registering\, you will receive a confirma
 tion email containing information about attending the library talk. Learn 
 about home gardening\, pest management\, water conservation practices\, an
 d more from your Sonoma County UC Master Gardeners! Different presentation
  topic per location.
LOCATION:Northwest Santa Rosa Library
URL:https://events.sonomalibrary.org/event/uc-master-gardeners-all-about-g
 rowing-beautiful-orchids-117790
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
