UID:261106jYL1vI7UMEK9ln-jW4xuLw
DESCRIPTION:In this class\, students will learn the art of basket twining 
 to crest a unique basket. Students will be using Japanese paper cord\, and
  will learn to lay out spoke\, twine around them\, add color\, and create 
 a polished finishing look.\n\nAll Materials Provided.\n\nThere will be dis
 cussion breaks throughout the class\, as well as a lunch break. Please bri
 ng a paper bag lunch.\n\nAbout the Teacher: Carrie Botto is a self taught 
 multi-medium weaver. She started weaving with beads over 40 years ago and 
 continues to add skills and techniques to her “tool box”. Carrie trave
 ls all over the country now teaching several different classes\, and has t
 aught at Mendocino Art Center\, New Mexico Bead Trader\, Moab Art Center\,
  and Fiber on 4th in New Mexico. Follow Carrie on Instagram @beanstreetsud
 io!
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/paper-basket-twining
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
