BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T170000
UID:261004rEZJi0--TUWT3pEOYfK1BQ
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crossing Delancey - a Curtain Call Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T160000
UID:261107zguNveAXgE2UHAUdobELGA
DESCRIPTION:She knows exactly the kind of guy she wants\, but grandmother 
 Bubbe and the matchmaker think differently. \n\nThis nostalgic favorite w
 as made into a beloved film in 1988. It is a love story about Izzy\, a tho
 roughly modern woman with not the greatest taste in men. Her grandmother B
 ubbe is desperate to get her married. Enter Henka\, the matchmaker with a 
 New York accent so sharp it could cut cheese\, and Sam Posner\, the pickle
  man with the heart of a poet. Will Izzy make the right choice? Doors open
  half an hour early for a photographic slideshow about New York’s Lower 
 East Side\, and some special snacks: Babka and Brooklyn Egg Creams. Don’
 t miss this delightful romantic comedy suitable for ages 8 and up. \n\nPl
 aywright: Susan Sandler\n\nDirector: Amanda Claiborne\n\nStarring: Kathy P
 ing-Rogers\, Kimy Martinez-Knight\, Nick Stewart\, Karen Clancy and Jake H
 amlin\n\n**Trigger warnings:** Mention of suicide and some mild cursing in
  Yiddish. Suitable for ages 8 and up.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre Russian River Hall
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
