BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Kabbalah of Meaning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T193000
UID:261001Oxp049BDTUG1OoOcT4DwQQ
DESCRIPTION:Jewish Wisdom for a Life That Matters\n\nNo matter how much we
  achieve\, something within us still asks: “Is this it? Isn’t there so
 mething more?”\n\nThe Kabbalah of Meaning is a new six-session JLI cours
 e exploring the Jewish answer to that question. What are we really searchi
 ng for—and where can it be found?\n\nDrawing on Kabbalah and centuries o
 f Jewish wisdom\, we’ll uncover the essential building blocks of a deepl
 y meaningful life. We’ll explore how purpose can be found in our work\, 
 relationships\, challenges\, accomplishments\, and even the ordinary routi
 nes that fill our days.\n\nYou don’t have to revamp your life. You don
 ’t need to meditate on a mountaintop. You simply need a new lens through
  which to see the rich world of meaning already woven into every part of y
 our life.\n\nThoughtful\, practical\, and surprisingly relevant\, this cou
 rse offers fresh perspectives and useful tools for living with greater cla
 rity\, connection\, and intention.\n\nTry 1st class free.\n\nNo previous J
 ewish learning required. Come as you are—and bring your questions.
LOCATION:Chabad Jewish Center of Petaluma
URL:https://www.jewishpetaluma.com/templates/articlecco_cdo/aid/7522546/je
 wish/The-Kabbalah-of-Meaning.htm
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vallejo Hike Club's Tuesday Evening Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T193000
UID:2609305uKfGykmwUSDj8EOsMnD1g
DESCRIPTION:Join us every Tuesday evening at 6:00 pm for a relaxing hike a
 long the Vallejo waterfront.\n\nThese hikes are beginner-friendly\, family
 -friendly\, dog-friendly and welcoming to all fitness levels! It will be a
  time to relax\, reset\, and focus on enjoying good company\, and peaceful
  transition from work into the rest of your evening.\n\nWhether you're new
  to hiking\, looking to meet new friends\, or simply want a healthy way to
  decompress\, we'd love to have you with us. Let's enjoy Vallejo's trails 
 together. See you Tuesday!\n\nEvery evening\, 6:00 pm to 7:30 pm. Meetup a
 t the Vallejo ferry terminal\, Vallejo.
LOCATION:Vallejo Ferry Terminal
URL:https://www.rootedvallejo.com/what-we-do/vallejo-hike-club
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music Happy Hour - The Hutchinsons: Sonoma Seasoned Americana
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T190000
UID:260906EzkQv6niWUil1_cVtSNegg
DESCRIPTION:For people who like to party...but want to be home at a reason
 able hour...\n\nThe Hutchinsons: Seasoned Americana - Every 1st Tuesday! C
 oming from the tradition of folk music\, Kevin Hutchinson is a musical sto
 ryteller. His influences and styles cover many genres: folk\, folk rock\, 
 blues\, rock\, rockabilly\, Americana\, country\, swing\, and\, of course\
 , folk. His music is lyric driven\, and spans topics from love to social c
 ommentary\, serious to light hearted.\n\nKevin loves connecting with the a
 udience with his originals and thoughtful covers of artists that have insp
 ired him\, often pulling from their lesser known material.\n\nArtistic inf
 luences\, covering decades\, include: John Prine\; Bob Dylan\; Bruce Cockb
 urn\; Warren Zevon\; Crosby\, Stills and Nash\; Peter\, Paul and Mary\; Ro
 bert Earl Keen\; Tom Russel\; Tom Paxton\; Paul Thorne\; and many more.\n\
 n21+ Happy Hour Pricing 4-7pm All beers - $6 + $2 off wine. Live Music 5-7
 pm 2 drink minimum\, please\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for
  all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/live-music-happy-hour-the-hutchinsons-son
 oma-seasoned-americana-tickets-1336190193839?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Salsa - Tuesdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T183000
UID:260705vgMzFmWKOkSauWa_K6Ex_A
DESCRIPTION:Ready to dance? Join our beginner salsa class where no experie
 nce or partner is needed. Just comfortable shoes and desire to have fun!\n
 \nGreat for first timers!\n\nNo dance experience required\n\nNon-marking s
 hoes soles\n\nNo partner necessary\n\nOur relaxed environment is perfect f
 or learning salsa basics\, as we make it fun and enjoyable. In this class 
 you will learn basic directional steps\, proper frame for partner-work and
  simple turn patterns. We organize our curriculum so that the movements ar
 e easy to remember. Join us to learn the fundamentals! No experience is ne
 cessary and no partner is required. Drop-in fee is $20.\n\nDate & Time: Tu
 esdays @ 5:30PM – 6:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/beginner-salsa-tuesdays
 /17157360/2026-12-01T17
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261201T193000
UID:260704NSzq4rG4B0C4mYLfF5vCwg
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 6:30PM – 7:30PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/intermediate-salsa-clas
 s/17159571/2026-12-01T18
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
