BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"People of the West: Gold Rush" Screening\, Presentation & Nature 
 Walk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T200000
UID:261106Vv0Pu0BNn0mEoURJTXDGnA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our third “People of the West” screening\, whe
 re we watch the "Gold Rush" episode\, which covers California's mid-1800s 
 transformation — marked by conquest\, massacres\, and betrayal. Followin
 g the presentation and discussion\, participants will hear a half-hour pre
 sentation by Archaeologist Mark Selverston on research and cultural resour
 ce projects he's undertaken at prominent Gold Rush and state park location
 s. We'll then have the opportunity to take part in a gentle walk along the
  Copeland Creek Trail to the Native Plant Garden\, where we can rest and r
 eflect with nature. Dinner will be provided!
LOCATION:SSU Stevenson Hall 1301 and Native Plant Garden
URL:https://cei.sonoma.edu/gold-rush
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Salsa Intermediate with Steven Khuong (6 Weeks)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T191500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T201500
UID:261019blKjcg9gIEKUlQKqsde0sA
DESCRIPTION:December 2 – January 6 \\(6 weeks\\)\n\n7:15 PM – 8:15 PM 
 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8\, San Rafael\, CA\n\nReady to take your salsa to
  the next level? This 6-week salsa intermediate Marin series is designed f
 or dancers who already know the basics \\(timing\, basic steps\, and simpl
 e turns\, etc.\\) and want to build the confidence and versatility to shin
 e on the social dance floor.\n\nIn this class\, you’ll:\n\nDevelop adapt
 ability so you can flow with different partners and music.\n\nRefine your 
 footwork and styling for sharper expression.\n\nMaster more complex turn p
 atterns and combinations.\n\nStrengthen your lead and follow for smoother\
 , more connected dancing.\n\nWhat to Expect: Steven’s teaching style ble
 nds structure with fun\, creating a supportive space where you’ll be cha
 llenged but never overwhelmed. Each week builds on the last\, helping you 
 progress steadily while keeping the joy of salsa front and center.\n\nDeta
 ils:\n\nNo partner necessary — rotations ensure everyone gets to dance.\
 n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe soles to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10
  minutes early to warm up and get settled.\n\nDate & Time: Wednesdays @ 7:
 15PM – 8:15PM\n\nInstructor: Steven Khuong\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood High
 way \\#8 San Rafael\, CA
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/intermediate-salsa-wednesday-715-pm/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bottega Cellar Series with Stony Hill Vineyard & Heitz Cellar
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T210000
UID:261006Lcv1_933GUuorYN7APzX_A
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Bottega on December 2nd for an elegant evening feat
 uring Stony Hill Vineyard and Heitz Cellar\, hosted by Carlton McCoy Jr.\,
  Master Sommelier and CEO of Lawrence Wine Estates. Lawrence Wine Estates'
  Stony Hill Vineyard and Heitz Cellar are two of Napa Valley's most storie
 d wineries. Founded on Spring Mountain in 1952 by the McCrea family\, Ston
 y Hill built its legacy on high-elevation Chardonnay and Riesling\, becomi
 ng known as one of America's great white wine producers. Heitz Cellar\, fo
 unded in 1961 by Joe and Alice Heitz\, pioneered single-vineyard designate
 d wines with Napa's first vineyard-designated Cabernet Sauvignon\, helping
  establish the very idea of site-specific terroir in the valley. Hosted by
  the dynamic Carlton McCoy\, Master Sommelier and CEO of Lawrence Wine Est
 ates. Guests will experience a thoughtfully curated progression of wines h
 ighlighting two of Napa Valley’s most distinctive wineries\, moving from
  expressive Chardonnay to a remarkable selection of Cabernet Sauvignon fro
 m Spring Mountain\, Rutherford\, and Oakville. The wines will be paired wi
 th a seasonal multi-course menu by Bottega Executive Chef Alex Espinoza\, 
 with each course designed to complement their character and expression whi
 le showcasing refined flavors\, exceptional ingredients\, and the gracious
  hospitality that defines Bottega.\n\nPrice is inclusive of tax and gratui
 ty.\n\n6525 Washington Street Suite A9\, Yountville\, CA 94599\n\n(707) 94
 5-1050
LOCATION:Bottega Napa Valley
URL:https://www.opentable.com/booking/experiences-availability?rid=25489&r
 estref=25489&experienceId=791062&utm_source=external&utm_medium=referral&u
 tm_campaign=shared
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Handbuilding: Here Comes the Holidays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T130000
UID:260928qeVnK3IktUKZyjI7414R_g
DESCRIPTION:Wednesdays Weekly · 8 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nOctober 7 – D
 ecember 2\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nExceptions\n\nNo class Novembe
 r 11\, Veterans Day\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nCategory\
 n\nCeramics\, Extended Classes\, Handcrafted for the Holidays\n\nExperienc
 e Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$265\n\nMa
 terials Fee:\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$295\n\nThis 8 week ses
 sion with our pottery texture queen\, Lynn Wood\, will be slab based with 
 focus on the holidays. The projects will center around creating forms for
  celebrating including serving dishes\, decorative surfaces\, holiday the
 med gifts and more. This class will help you get started early and be pr
 epared for gift giving and holiday success. Everyone will learn to make a 
 new lantern. Fun and laughs will also be included.\n\nInterested in spendi
 ng a bit more time in the studio with Lynn Wood? This session\, opt-in for
  and additional 1.5 hours of guided working time each class session in the
  studio with Lynn Wood for an extra fee. Regularly scheduled class will oc
 cur from 10am-1pm\, and then our additional Guided Working Session with Ly
 nn Wood will run from 1:30pm-3:00pm
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
