BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Remission Reimagined: Art\, Healing & Connection
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T120000
UID:261107MWMtTtvlBkmnPlaZ4e829w
DESCRIPTION:Remission Reimagined is a supportive\, community-based worksho
 p that brings together individuals who have experienced cancer and are int
 erested in exploring the role art has played in their lives. Through shari
 ng artwork\, personal stories\, creative processes\, and artistic techniqu
 es\, participants will have the opportunity to connect with others who hav
 e navigated similar experiences and participate in multi-media art-making.
 \n\nA $5 materials fee due will be collected at the start of class.\n\nAbo
 ut Cathryn Hudin \n\nCathryn is an accomplished\, professional ceramic art
 ist whose distinguished career spans several decades. She has served as an
  instructor and President of Board of Directors at Paradise Art Center and
  has taught ceramics at Butte College and California State University\, Ch
 ico. Through her participation in the Artists-in-Schools Program\, she has
  shared her passion for art with students and inspired the next generation
  of artists. A cancer survivor\, Cathryn embodies resilience and persevera
 nce\, qualities that inform her life\, her work and her endearing commitme
 nt to the arts.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center - Gallery (standing room)
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/remission-reimagined-art-h
 ealing-connection?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261202T000000
UID:260606e3NMJduxdES4OquqCshsTw
DESCRIPTION:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market is a year-rou
 nd Saturday tradition in Sonoma County\, bringing together local farmers\,
  ranchers\, food artisans\, and neighbors from 8:30 a.m. to 1 p.m. This is
  not just a place to shop\, it's a place to connect directly with the peop
 le who grow your food. As a Slow Food Sonoma County award recipient\, the 
 market prioritizes integrity\, seasonality\, and true farm-to-community re
 lationships. Expect peak-season produce harvested just hours before market
 \, pasture-raised meats\, fresh flowers\, artisan breads\, handcrafted goo
 ds\, and thoughtfully prepared foods that reflect the region's agricultura
 l richness. Visitors can stroll the vibrant open-air market\, sample local
  flavors\, and experience Sonoma County's food culture in its most authent
 ic form. Families\, chefs\, and weekend explorers alike gather here to dis
 cover what's growing now and to support small farms that keep our local fo
 od system strong. Open every Saturday\, rain or shine\, the Santa Rosa Ori
 ginal Certified Farmers Market is a cornerstone of the community and a mus
 t-visit stop for anyone wanting to taste\, shop\, and experience Sonoma Co
 unty at its freshest.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
