BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Laguna Stewards Day/ Dia de Laguna Stewards at Colgan Creek
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T123000
UID:261101aGdSO8s3jUCjHcMzjEHS1Q
DESCRIPTION:Join the Laguna de Santa Rosa Foundation and City of Santa Ros
 a at Lower Colgan Creek for a hands-on stewardship day! Help create Santa 
 Rosa’s first Monarch Meadows by planting milkweed and native wildflowers
  to support monarch butterflies\, bees\, and other pollinators. Connect wi
 th nature\, meet your neighbors\, and help create a lasting habitat for lo
 cal wildlife! We suggest wearing layers as it may be cold in the morning\,
  long pants\, closed-toe shoes\, and sun protection. Bring a backpack\, an
 d a water bottle\; we’ll bring the tools\, gloves\, extra water\, and sn
 acks. Only heavy rain cancels. All ages are welcome!\n\nBig thank you to o
 ur Phase 3 project funders\, which include the Department of Water Resourc
 es Urban Streams Restoration Program\, the Wildlife Conservation Board\, a
 nd the Sonoma County Agricultural Preservation and Open Space District. Ad
 ditional Phase 3 partners include the City of Santa Rosa and Rainforest Ri
 sing. Thank you Xerces Society for Invertebrate Conservation for the habit
 at kits. We could not do this work without them.\n\n¡Únete a la Fundaci
 ón Laguna de Santa Rosa y a la Ciudad de Santa Rosa en Lower Colgan Creek
  para un día de voluntariado y conservación! Ayúdanos a crear los prime
 ros Prados de Mariposas Monarca de Santa Rosa\, plantando algodoncillo y f
 lores silvestres nativas para apoyar a las mariposas monarca\, las abejas 
 y otros polinizadores. ¡Conéctate con la naturaleza\, conoce a tus vecin
 os y contribuye a crear un hábitat duradero para la fauna local! Sugerimo
 s usar pantalones largos\, zapatos cerrados y protección solar. Se recomi
 enda traer una mochila y una botella de agua\; nosotros llevaremos las her
 ramientas\, los guantes\, agua extra y refrigerios. Solo se cancela por ll
 uvia intensa. ¡Son bienvenidas personas de todas las edades!\n\nAgradecem
 os enormemente a los financiadores de la Fase 3 del proyecto\, entre ellos
  el Programa de Restauración de Arroyos Urbanos del Departamento de Recur
 sos Hídricos\, la Junta de Conservación de la Vida Silvestre y el Distri
 to de Preservación Agrícola y Espacios Abiertos del Condado de Sonoma. O
 tros socios de la Fase 3 incluyen la Ciudad de Santa Rosa y Rainforest Ris
 ing. Gracias a Xerces Society for Invertebrate Conservation por los kits d
 e hábitat. ¡Sin ellos\, no podríamos realizar este trabajo!
LOCATION:Lower Colgan Creek
URL:https://lagunastewards12526.eventbrite.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monica Da Silva & Complicated Animals
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T170000
UID:261031xb39ShRKrkie-h-2JFvFwA
DESCRIPTION:Monica da Silva grew up living between The United States and B
 elém\, Brazil\, a city on the Amazon River. A love of travel and foreign 
 language helped to forge her unique sound. \n\n \n\nParalleling her life\,
  da Silva's music contains an eclectic mix of Brazilian and American influ
 ences. Her sound can be classified as International Fusion\, as it is heav
 ily influenced by Brazilian music\, namely Bossa Nova\, but also incorpora
 tes elements of Lounge\, Electronica\, Indie Pop\, and Worldbeat. Da Silva
  brings her cultural diversity to her songs\, smoothly flowing between Eng
 lish\, Portuguese\, and Spanish.\n\n \n\nIn 2010\, da Silva released her a
 lbum "Brasilissima" . The record featured songs in both of her native lang
 uages - English and Portuguese. The first single "Aí Então"\, “was cho
 sen by Putumayo World Music to be included on their compilation “Brazili
 an Beat”. The upbeat\, psychedelic track "That's Not The Way" was chosen
  by the music director of ESPN to be played during the programming of The 
 FIFA World Cup in 2014\, alongside major recording artists Coldplay\, Sér
 gio Mendes\, Pitbull\, Jennifer Lopez\, The Black Eyed Peas\, Stan Getz\, 
 and Astrud Gilberto. \n\nDa Silva's single "Soldado de Amor" \\(2017\\) ha
 s been featured in the BBC One series "The Replacement”\, in the Paramou
 nt Network series "American Woman"\, and in a 2019 campaign for the design
 er Tory Burch.\n\nHer music has also been featured in the series "Heartlan
 d"\, and in an ad for Patron Tequila. She is currently recording a new\, f
 ull-length solo album\, as well as writing and recording with her project\
 , Complicated Animals.
