BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crossing Delancey - a Curtain Call Theatre Production
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T163000
UID:261107JGK2-knl90Wzt1Jeq-sB3w
DESCRIPTION:She knows exactly the kind of guy she wants\, but grandmother 
 Bubbe and the matchmaker think differently. \n\nThis nostalgic favorite w
 as made into a beloved film in 1988. It is a love story about Izzy\, a tho
 roughly modern woman with not the greatest taste in men. Her grandmother B
 ubbe is desperate to get her married. Enter Henka\, the matchmaker with a 
 New York accent so sharp it could cut cheese\, and Sam Posner\, the pickle
  man with the heart of a poet. Will Izzy make the right choice? Doors open
  half an hour early for a photographic slideshow about New York’s Lower 
 East Side\, and some special snacks: Babka and Brooklyn Egg Creams. Don’
 t miss this delightful romantic comedy suitable for ages 8 and up. \n\nPl
 aywright: Susan Sandler\n\nDirector: Amanda Claiborne\n\nStarring: Kathy P
 ing-Rogers\, Kimy Martinez-Knight\, Nick Stewart\, Karen Clancy and Jake H
 amlin\n\n**Trigger warnings:** Mention of suicide and some mild cursing in
  Yiddish. Suitable for ages 8 and up.
LOCATION:Curtain Call Theatre Russian River Hall
URL:https://www.russianriverhall.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music Happy Hour - The Ukulele Ramblers - Open Uke Jam!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T180000
UID:26110781waTlJTMk-ZNmDZVMhJ3Q
DESCRIPTION:Saturday afternoons hit differently at Barrel Proof Lounge.\n\
 nWe open early — 3pm — and hand the room over to Ukulele Ramblers\, a 
 friendly\, talented ukulele collective that turns Happy Hour into a laid-b
 ack\, sing-along hang.\n\nThis is live music and an open uke jam. Bring yo
 ur ukulele if you’ve got one. Bring your voice even if you don’t. The 
 Ramblers lead the way with familiar tunes\, easy harmonies\, and a welcomi
 ng vibe that makes it just as fun to join in as it is to sit back and list
 en.\n\nNo pressure. No ego. Just good songs\, good people\, and a room tha
 t feels like it belongs to everyone.\n\n Live Music & Open Uke Jam | 3–
 6pm  Happy Hour drinks  Free popcorn  21+\n\n Barrel Proof Lounge 501 
 Mendocino Avenue\, Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nIt’s the kind of afternoon you
  plan to stop by for one drink… and somehow stay for three hours.\n\n**w
 ww.UkuleleRamblers.net**\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for al
 l sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/live-music-happy-hour-the-ukulele-rambler
 s-open-uke-jam-tickets-1485589782029?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Headline Comedy: Luke Severeid LIVE! – Downtown Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T210000
UID:261106PgmTihzrs069-xIeCatbYQ
DESCRIPTION:Headline Comedy: Luke Severeid LIVE!\n\nSaturday\, December 5 
 | 7 PM | Barrel Proof Lounge | Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nHalf a million follo
 wers. Sold-out international shows. Two comedy specials with KNOTFEST. One
  very loud Saturday night in Santa Rosa.\n\nSeattle comedian Luke Severeid
  is bringing his gloriously unhinged brand of stand-up comedy to Barrel Pr
 oof Lounge for a special Saturday edition of Headline Comedy!\n\nBald\, be
 arded\, metal-headed\, and built like your favorite band's former bass pla
 yer\, Luke is a walking collision of heavy metal energy\, absurd observati
 ons\, and hilariously chaotic storytelling.\n\nHis comedy has been describ
 ed as "aggressively absurd\," "idiotically insightful\," and perhaps most 
 accurately\, "unmedicated ADHD in action." And somehow\, it all makes perf
 ect sense when he's holding a microphone.\n\nWith over 500\,000 followers 
 online\, Luke has taken his comedy around the world\, including a sold-out
  Australian tour as part of KNOTFEST\, the legendary heavy metal music fes
 tival.\n\nHe's also recorded two stand-up comedy specials in Minneapolis\,
  set to become KNOTFEST's first-ever stand-up comedy special releases.\n\n
 Luke's comedy hits like a guitar solo you didn't see coming. Loud\, fast\,
  ridiculous\, and surprisingly insightful. He's got the energy of a metal 
 frontman and the comedic instincts to turn everyday absurdity into somethi
 ng spectacularly funny.\n\nThis is exactly why we do Headline Comedy. Bigg
 er acts\, special Saturday shows\, and comedians worth making a night out 
 for.\n\nShow Details\n\nSaturday\, December 5\, 2026\n\nBarrel Proof Loung
 e – 501 Mendocino Ave\, Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nShowtime: 7 PM\n\n21+ Onl
 y\n\nCome see why hundreds of thousands of fans are following this magnifi
 cent\, bearded lunatic.\n\nHe will make you laugh. Loudly.\n\nCheck out **
 www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://Severeid.eventbrite.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Merry & Bright
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T190000
UID:2611067fOO56N9JECsP_uybnwsgQ
DESCRIPTION:**Step into Santa Rosa’s premier winter wonderland for the 6
 th Annual *Merry & Bright*!**\n\nPresented by Sonoma Clean Power\, produce
 d by the Redwood Ice Theatre Company (RITC)\, and hosted at iconic Snoopy
 ’s Home Ice\, this cherished holiday tradition returns with nine complet
 ely free outdoor ice skating shows. Gather the family to watch dazzling ro
 utines from professional skaters\, accompanied by classic holiday music an
 d seasonal entertainment designed to bring neighbors together across Sonom
 a and Mendocino counties.\n\nIn the spirit of innovation and sustainabilit
 y\, this year’s outdoor production is powered directly by Sonoma Clean P
 ower’s all-electric Ford F-150 Lightning truck—showcasing clean energy
  in action while helping local households discover easy ways to save energ
 y this winter.\n\n**Admission:** Completely free\, no tickets required!\n\
 n**Location:** Snoopy’s Home Ice\, Santa Rosa\n\n**Show Schedule (9 Free
  Outdoor Performances):**\n\n**Friday\, December 4:** 5:00 p.m. & 6:00 p.m
 .\n\n**Saturday\, December 5:** 2:00 p.m.\, 3:00 p.m.\, 5:00 p.m. & 6:00 p
 .m.\n\n**Sunday\, December 6:** 1:00 p.m.\, 2:00 p.m. & 3:00 p.m.\n\n**Pro
  Tip:** Arrive early to bundle up\, grab a hot cocoa\, and secure the best
  spot to watch the show!\n\nTo learn more about how SCP is giving back thi
 s holiday season\, visit: https://sonomacleanpower.org/holidays
LOCATION:Snoopy's Home Ice
URL:https://sonomacleanpower.org/holidays
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
